{
  "$comment": [
    "The Protein Viewer Pack's published source (PT-9911): every file the publisher's extract (not published) takes from a commit, read from that same commit. A file not named here is never extracted.",
    "Paths are repository paths. `trees`: a directory and everything under it (the vendored PyMOL runtime only). `files`: one file each, published where it is. `root`: a file published at the top of the extract under the name given (README.md, LICENSE).",
    "`decide`: directories whose every file, at any depth, is decided one by one: published (`files`, `root`) or `withheld` (path, or a directory ending in `/`, with the reason; a file named in `files` under a withheld directory is published). The extractor refuses a commit with an undecided file there, and extract.test.ts the working tree (PT-10171).",
    "`transforms`: a file in `files` written changed: `strings` keeps the keys stringFilters.ts lets the offline file carry; `css-prune` keeps the rules a published source file can match (vite-plugins/gantt-css-prune.ts), without comments. They run when the extract is finished, on the packages the extract's lockfile pins.",
    "`shims`: a module written in place of one the published source does not carry, re-exporting the offline file's own stand-in for it (aliases.ts).",
    "`package`: the extract's frontend/package.json. Versions are not kept here: each package's version, and the lockfile, come from frontend/package-lock.json at the same commit.",
    "standalone/structure-viewer/source/extract.test.ts checks that the extract is closed under its imports, decided file by file, and carries its licences; the publisher's clean build (not published) cuts, finishes, scans, builds and tests it in a clean container; source/scan-reviewed.json lists the third-party files whose generic scan hits were read and accepted."
  ],
